WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.230
After all the smoke settled and all the cool
hand signals were waved, Doctor Stephen Strange

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:09.440
earned his spot as one of the Marvel Cinematic
Universe's best new heroes.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.009
And like in other Marvel movies, we got an
extra helping of heroism in the form of teasers

00:00:13.009 --> 00:00:15.639
for future films after the movie's ending.

00:00:15.639 --> 00:00:18.970
Put on your Sling Ring as we explore Doctor
Strange's credits scenes.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:22.300
And just so you don't think we're possessed
by the dark powers of Dormammu, here's our

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:25.730
warning: there are major spoilers ahead.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:26.849
Thor's Doctor visit

00:00:26.849 --> 00:00:30.779
It's Hammer Time once again as Odin's favorite
son makes a long-awaited return after his

00:00:30.779 --> 00:00:32.800
absence from Captain America: Civil War.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.710
The blond brute doesn't look as heroic as
usual when he visits Stephen at his Sanctum.

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:41.361
After getting the Asgardian a giant, magically-refilling
beer, Strange gets down to brass tacks: he

00:00:41.361 --> 00:00:45.660
now keeps track of major otherworldly threats
to Earth, which includes Thor's brother Loki,

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:49.160
who has accompanied Thor to New York to look
for their missing daddy, Odin.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:52.981
For the sake of getting Loki off Earth and
back to Asgard as soon as possible, Strange

00:00:52.981 --> 00:00:55.430
decides to help the Odinsons look for their
missing patriarch.

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.430
We've still got a lot of questions about what's
happened in Thor's absence,

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:02.310
"Am I disappointed that they didn't invite
me to fight with them?

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:04.740
Um, ha no."

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:06.860
"He doesn't know how to get in touch with
you."

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:08.110
"I don't have a phone."

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:09.310
"He doesn't have a phone!"

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:12.330
...but we have a feeling Thor: Ragnarok will
have answers.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.630
And probably lots of smashing.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:15.690
"Well they're excited."

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.210
Loki's back in town

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:25.270
The last time we saw Loki in Thor: The Dark
World, he was sitting on the throne of Asgard

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:28.170
disguised as Odin, after faking his own death.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:32.101
Thor didn't seem to notice it was actually
Loki, especially when the "King" offered him

00:01:32.101 --> 00:01:34.290
the throne of Asgard, which Thor declined.

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:39.070
He even showed sadness in describing Loki's
death, which shows Loki that Thor still ultimately

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:40.070
cares.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:42.780
We're not sure what happened after that: Did
Thor see through Loki's disguise?

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:44.810
Did the real Odin contact Thor?

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:49.420
Or, even more crazy: Is it not even Thor at
all, but actually Loki impersonating him to

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:51.120
fool Doctor Strange?

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:55.540
One thing's for sure: the last time Loki was
in New York, things were kind of...bad.

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:05.320
Next time, just take a taxi, dude.

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:06.920
Ragnarok and roll call

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:10.429
Tossing the Sorcerer Supreme into the mix
of Thor: Ragnarok is going to make for some

00:02:10.429 --> 00:02:12.290
interesting events.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:15.519
Considering Marvel has teased that part of
World War Hulk will be mixed into Ragnarok,

00:02:15.519 --> 00:02:18.620
we can't wait to see what happens when Doctor
Strange meets Doctor Banner.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:22.319
"I'm sorry, I'm not that kind of doctor.

00:02:22.319 --> 00:02:24.599
I'm not a therapist, it's not my training."

00:02:24.599 --> 00:02:25.099
"So."

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:25.660
"I don't have the-"

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:26.800
"What, the time?"

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:28.460
"Temperament."

00:02:28.739 --> 00:02:32.670
Ragnarok director Taika Waititi supposedly
played a huge role in the filming of the mid-credits

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:36.499
sequence, so will the Master of the Mystic
Arts throw down with the Hulk?

00:02:36.499 --> 00:02:39.709
It's probably worth noting that in the comics,
Strange was one of the people responsible

00:02:39.709 --> 00:02:43.269
for exiling the Hulk into space, setting up
the events of the World War Hulk story in

00:02:43.269 --> 00:02:44.909
the first place.

00:02:44.909 --> 00:02:46.540
Just a stone's throw away...

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:50.400
Thor interacting with Doctor Strange inadvertently
increases the chances of bringing multiple

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.109
Infinity Stones together.

00:02:52.109 --> 00:02:56.529
For now, Strange leaves the Time Stone-slash-Eye
of Agamotto in Kamar-Taj, which magically

00:02:56.529 --> 00:02:58.239
connects to his New York Sanctum.

00:02:58.239 --> 00:03:02.499
Likewise, the Space Stone-slash-Tesseract
is now in the vaults of Asgard under heavy

00:03:02.499 --> 00:03:03.579
protection.

00:03:03.579 --> 00:03:07.379
Putting Strange in Thor's third solo film
moves these Infinity Stones awfully close

00:03:07.379 --> 00:03:08.379
together.

00:03:08.379 --> 00:03:11.590
The Doc will undoubtedly learn more from Wong
about the Infinity Stones, and there's bound

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:14.769
to be some kind of crazy spell that Strange
could use to find out where the other Stones

00:03:14.769 --> 00:03:18.069
are—just to make sure they're all properly
accounted for and in the right hands.

00:03:18.069 --> 00:03:21.049
Of course, someone else is on the lookout
for them too…

00:03:21.049 --> 00:03:22.519
Thanos on the hunt

00:03:22.519 --> 00:03:25.730
Thanos has finally stepped off his floating
throne and started looking for the Infinity

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:30.680
Stones himself...which still seems weird considering
he presumably gave Loki the staff containing

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:31.760
the Mind Stone.

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:36.329
Thor: Ragnarok isn't hitting theaters until
November 3, 2017, and Avengers: Infinity War

00:03:36.329 --> 00:03:41.049
is scheduled for May 4, 2018, so this could
be the perfect opportunity for Thanos to start

00:03:41.049 --> 00:03:42.810
decorating his golden glove.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:46.719
Some fans believe Heimdall carries the Soul
Stone in his armor, which explains how he

00:03:46.719 --> 00:03:48.469
can see every person in the Nine Realms.

00:03:48.469 --> 00:03:52.269
A Thor-Strange team-up could potentially tie
together half of the Stones.

00:03:52.269 --> 00:03:56.669
Don't be surprised if the Mad Titan nabs a
few before Infinity War even begins.

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:58.040
Setting up a sequel

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:02.019
Instead of teasing another superhero crossover,
the post-credits scenes established a subplot

00:04:02.019 --> 00:04:05.029
that sets up the Sorcerer Supreme's inevitable
sophomore film.

00:04:05.029 --> 00:04:08.279
Mordo, the sorcerer who abandoned Doctor Strange
at the end of the film for his abuse of the

00:04:08.279 --> 00:04:11.159
Time Stone, visits Jonathan Pangborn.

00:04:11.159 --> 00:04:14.749
Pangborn was once paralyzed, but headed overseas
to Kamar-Taj, where he learned how to magically

00:04:14.749 --> 00:04:16.560
restore his ability to walk.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:20.349
Mordo attacks Pangborn, draining him of his
magical powers, and revealing a huge change

00:04:20.349 --> 00:04:22.509
in character and a dangerous vendetta.

00:04:22.509 --> 00:04:25.620
He's decided that there are just way too many
dang sorcerers bending the rules—so it's

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:27.440
up to him to whittle down their numbers.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:31.730
He'll inevitably cross paths with the likes
of Wong and Stephen Strange once again.

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:33.120
Mordo the villain

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:36.620
Fans of the printed version of Doctor Strange
knew this switcheroo was coming, despite Mordo

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:39.720
being made into a supportive character throughout
most of the film.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:43.180
Even when he parts ways with Strange, it's
mostly out of angry disillusionment.

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:47.400
In the comics, Baron Mordo is a longtime antagonist
to Doctor Strange.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:50.620
Originally a student of the Ancient One, Mordo
tries to kill his master after growing jealous

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:54.069
of Strange becoming a star pupil, leading
to his banishment and pursuit of the black

00:04:54.069 --> 00:04:57.560
arts and other forbidden forms of magic in
order to achieve power.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:01.240
Of course, many of these techniques can backfire,
which is kind of what happened with Kaecilius,

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:04.960
who is originally only a bottom-tier flunky
of Mordo's in the comics.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:08.020
Despite his change and his crusade against
other sorcerers, it's not like Mordo's gone

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:09.150
fully evil.

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:11.590
He could've simply killed Pangborn if he wanted.

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:13.120
Silencing the sorcerers

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:17.180
Mordo siphoning Pangborn's magical powers
foreshadows his inevitable showdown against

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:18.180
Strange.

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.750
His exchange with Pangborn suggests that Mordo
is coming to terms with sorcerers bending

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:21.750
the laws of the universe.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:25.960
But he likely also believes that he's the
only person responsible enough to do the job.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:29.689
Mordo is out stealing sorcerers' magic powers
to try and bring things back to normal, and

00:05:29.689 --> 00:05:34.110
it should lead up to one heck of a fight in
Doctor Strange 2: Doctor Stranger.

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:35.130
Thanks for watching!

